{
  "name": "Google Sheets to WhatsApp: send a template to each new row and mark it sent",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Send a WhatsApp template to each new Google Sheets row\n\n### How it works\n1. Every 5 minutes, **Read the sheet** reads your Google Sheet. **Rows not sent yet** keeps each row with a phone number and no status, and **At most 50 a run** caps the batch.\n2. **Send WhatsApp template** sends your approved template through Cosend, with the row's name in the message.\n3. **Write the status** writes **sent** and the time into that row, or **failed** and Cosend's reason, so every row is sent once and you can see what happened.\n\n### Setup\n1. On self-hosted n8n, install the community node **n8n-nodes-cosend** (Settings > Community nodes), following n8n's [community node installation guide](https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/community-nodes/installation/).\n2. Make a sheet with a header row of **phone** and **name**. The workflow adds **status**, **sent_at** and **error** the first time it writes.\n3. In **Read the sheet**, connect Google and pick your sheet. Pick the same Google account in **Write the status**.\n4. In **Send WhatsApp template**, add a **Cosend API** credential with an API key from the Cosend dashboard (Settings > Developer > API keys), then pick your template and its language. With a workspace key, also pick the sending number in **Connection**.\n5. Turn the workflow on.\n\n### Customization\nChange how often it runs in **Every 5 minutes**, and how many rows a run sends in **At most 50 a run** (rename it to match). To send a row again, clear its **status**.\n\nTested with n8n-nodes-cosend 2026.11.0 on self-hosted n8n 2.46.6.",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "3f1c2b7a-5d1e-4c2a-9a51-0b7e3c1d2a01",
      "name": "About this workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -760,
        -280
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Read the rows to send\nWrite each number with its country code, for example **+44 7700 900123**; spaces and dashes are fine. A row with any status is skipped, and each run takes at most 50 rows.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 860,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "3f1c2b7a-5d1e-4c2a-9a51-0b7e3c1d2a02",
      "name": "Read the rows to send",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -80,
        -280
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Send the template\nCreate a template with one variable for the first name in the Cosend dashboard under **Templates**, for example *Hi {{1}}, thanks for signing up.* **Components** fills it from **name**. A template with no variables takes **[]**.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 340,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "3f1c2b7a-5d1e-4c2a-9a51-0b7e3c1d2a03",
      "name": "Send the template",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        800,
        -280
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Write the result\n**sent** means the message went out at the time in **sent_at**. **failed** puts Cosend's reason in **error**: fix the row, clear its status, and the next run sends it.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 600,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "3f1c2b7a-5d1e-4c2a-9a51-0b7e3c1d2a06",
      "name": "Write the result",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1160,
        -280
      ]
    },
    {
